摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"One portable memory layer for every AI agent: local-first, Markdown-native, user-owned, and self-evolving across apps, tools, and workflows.","id":"gh:1085086903","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"EverOS","slug":"EverMind-AI/EverOS","topics":["agent-memory","agentic-ai","ai","chats","clawdbot","clawdbot-skill","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","long-term-memory","mcp","memory","memory-management","python3","rag","skills"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"One portable memory layer for every AI agent: local-first, Markdown-native, user-owned, and self-evo"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"lving across apps, tools, and workflows."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Website · Documentation · Blog · 中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Table of Contents"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"- Why EverOS\n- Ecosystem Integrations\n- Quick Start\n- Use Cases\n- Documentation\n- EverMind Ecosystem"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"Ecosystem Integrations\n- Quick Start\n- Use Cases\n- Documentation\n- EverMind Ecosystem\n- Contributing"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Why EverOS"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"EverOS is a Python library and local-first memory runtime for agents and\nmakers. It gives one portab"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"le memory layer across coding assistants, apps,\ndevices, and workflows from day one. It stores conve"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"rsations, files, and agent\ntrajectories as readable Markdown, then syncs local SQLite and LanceDB in"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"dexes\nfor fast retrieval and self-evolving reuse."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Title\nEverOS\nOther Agent Memory Libraries"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Markdown source of truth\n✅ Canonical .md files that are readable, editable, diffable, and Git-versio"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ned\n❌ Usually API, vector, graph, dashboard, or database state"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Direct file editing\n✅ Edit .md files; cascade watcher syncs\n❌ Usually SDK, API, dashboard, or backen"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"iting\n✅ Edit .md files; cascade watcher syncs\n❌ Usually SDK, API, dashboard, or backend update paths"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Local three-part stack\n✅ Markdown + SQLite + LanceDB; no MongoDB, Elasticsearch, or Redis required\n❌"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" Often depends on managed services, vector DBs, graph DBs, or server stacks"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"User + agent tracks\n✅ User episodes/profile and agent cases/skills are separate first-class surfaces"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"\n❌ Usually centered on chat history, profiles, entities, facts, or retrieval records"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Orthogonal retrieval\n✅ Search by user_id, agent_id, app_id, project_id, and session_id\n❌ Usually app"},{"id":"p12s2","text":", namespace, tenant, thread, or graph scoped"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Knowledge Wiki\n✅ Editable, source-backed Markdown knowledge pages with taxonomy, CRUD APIs, and topi"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"c search\n❌ Usually separate from memory, trapped in a dashboard, or not tied back to source files"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Reflection\n✅ Offline memory evolution that merges episode clusters and refines profiles and skills b"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"etween sessions\n❌ Usually retrieval-only memory with little background consolidation or long-horizon"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ons\n❌ Usually retrieval-only memory with little background consolidation or long-horizon improvement"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Ecosystem Integrations"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"EverOS adds durable memory to the agent and workflow platforms below—and comes\nbuilt into Raven. Cho"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ose an integration to open its setup guide."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Hermes"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"OpenClaw"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Raven"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Dify"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> One OpenRouter API key is enough to start EverOS, write durable memories,\n> and retrieve them with"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" API key is enough to start EverOS, write durable memories,\n> and retrieve them with keyword search."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- Python 3.12+\n- One OpenRouter API key"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"### 1. Install"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### 2. Try the standalone demo — no key required"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"No API key or server setup required—run one command to quickly experience how\nEverOS stores and reca"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"or server setup required—run one command to quickly experience how\nEverOS stores and recalls memory:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Enter something EverOS should remember, then ask a related question to watch\nthe memory move through"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" ingest -> extract -> index -> recall."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"<https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98cb8e1e-2ca8-4504-b0a6-0b9a040a0a5c>"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### 3. Initialize and add your OpenRouter key"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"This creates `~/.everos/everos.toml` and `~/.everos/ome.toml`. Open\n`~/.everos/everos.toml`; the gen"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"erated model and OpenRouter URL are already\ncorrect, so replace only the empty `api_key`:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"This is the smallest Tier 1 setup: memory add, flush, Markdown persistence,\ncascade indexing, and ke"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"mallest Tier 1 setup: memory add, flush, Markdown persistence,\ncascade indexing, and keyword search."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Use `everos init --root <path>` if you want a different memory root. Pass the\nsame `--root <path>` t"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"o subsequent commands."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### 4. Start EverOS"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"Keep the server running, then open a second terminal and check it:"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"Look for `\"status\":\"ok\"`. With this one-key setup, `capabilities.embed` and\n`capabilities.rerank` re"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"main `false` until you configure them."},{"id":"p44s1","text":"### 5. Add and retrieve your first memory"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Business endpoints live under `/api/v2`. The older `/api/v1` prefix still\n> resolves to "},{"id":"p45s2","text":"the same handlers so existing integrations keep working, but it\n> is a legacy alias that may be remo"},{"id":"p45s3","text":"ved in a future major release — write new\n> code against `/api/v2`."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"Add a tiny conversation:"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"Flush the memory at the end of the session:"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"Search it back:"},{"id":"p51s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p52s1","text":"You should see the Yosemite memory in the response. Keep\n`\"method\": \"keyword\"` in this one-key setup"},{"id":"p52s2","text":" because the API defaults to hybrid\nsearch, which requires an embedding provider."},{"id":"p53s1","text":"> [!TIP]\n> **First memory unlocked.**\n> You just gave EverOS a fact, flushed it into durable Markdow"},{"id":"p53s2","text":"n-backed memory,\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p54s1","text":"### What works with one key?"},{"id":"p55s1","text":"The OpenRouter one-key setup is EverOS Tier 1. It supports server startup,\nmemory add and flush, dur"},{"id":"p55s2","text":"able Markdown storage, cascade indexing, and keyword\nsearch. Add optional providers only when you ne"},{"id":"p55s3","text":"ed the features below:"},{"id":"p56s1","text":"| Configuration | Adds |"},{"id":"p57s1","text":"| `[llm]` only | Core memory flow and keyword search |\n| Add `[embedding]` | Vector/user hybrid sear"},{"id":"p57s2","text":"ch, reflection, and skill extraction |\n| Add `[rerank]` too | Agentic search, default agent hybrid s"},{"id":"p57s3","text":"earch, and Knowledge Wiki |\n| Add `[multimodal]` and parser extra | Image, PDF, audio, and office-fi"},{"id":"p57s4","text":"wledge Wiki |\n| Add `[multimodal]` and parser extra | Image, PDF, audio, and office-file ingestion |"},{"id":"p58s1","text":"Missing optional capabilities are reported by `/health` and return a clear\nHTTP 422 if you request a"},{"id":"p58s2","text":" feature that needs them."},{"id":"p59s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> `everos demo --live` is different from the standalone demo in step 2: it\n> connects to a"},{"id":"p59s2","text":" running server and uses the real add/flush/search flow. It uses\n> hybrid search, so add an embeddin"},{"id":"p59s3","text":"g provider before you run it."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
